 "notes": [
  {
   "id": "31046949-624E-485F-89C6-2987333B5621",
   "rect": [
    [
     -40,
     -560
    ],
    [
     680,
     500
    ]
   ],
   "note": "# Glyph Carousel\n\n73 characters, each its own **3D Text Geometry** and **Instanced Mesh**, ride a ring of **radius** world units. The camera stands inside the ring just short of the rim, looking outward, so glyphs slide past from left to right a couple of units away. About five are in view at once; the other 68 or so are behind the camera or off to the sides.\n\nEvery glyph casts a shadow onto the floor from a point light and a directional light.\n\n**spin** sets the turning rate, **bob** floats each glyph, **size** scales them, **depth** flattens the extrusion."
  }
 ]
}